<title>USA: Trans World to buy headquarters building.</title>
<headline>Trans World to buy headquarters building.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS, Mo. 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Thursday it signed a contract to purchase a St. Louis County office building to house its world headquarters.</p>
<p>The building, with 87,000 square feet of space, was purchased from McDonnell Douglas Corp. It is located in Hazelwood, Mo., near TWA's other facilities at Lambert-St. Louis International Airport. Financial terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The airline will begin moving into the building this winter, with completion of the move expected in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>TWA said its lease at One City Centre in St. Louis would expire in February 1997.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
